[0mI don't see an AGENTS.md file in our chat. If you mean one from your own project, paste it here and I'll summarize it. If you mean the AGENTS.md format in general, here's the gist:

**AGENTS.md** is an open, simple convention for guiding AI coding agents, basically a "README for agents."

- **What it is:** A plain Markdown file at the root of a repository with instructions for AI coding tools. It has no required fields or schema.
- **Why it exists:** It keeps agent-specific details (exact commands, conventions, gotchas) out of the human-focused README and gives all tools one predictable place to look instead of separate config files for each.
- **Typical contents:** Setup, build, and test commands, code style rules, testing instructions, commit/PR guidelines, and security notes.
- **Nesting:** Monorepos can include AGENTS.md files in subfolders. The one closest to the file being edited takes precedence, and explicit user instructions override it.
- **Adoption:** It's supported by many tools, including OpenAI Codex, Cursor, Google's Jules, Amp, and Factory.
